# The application compatibility suite: one application per line, fields
# separated by "|":
#
#   name | installer file | sha256 | official URL | kind | install arguments
#        | installed program (Windows path) | launch arguments
#        | smoke command: PROGRAM::ARGUMENTS (optional) | smoke output must contain
#        | registry values set before installing (optional): KEY!NAME!TYPE!DATA,
#          several separated by ";" -- e.g. the policy that stops Firefox
#          updating itself mid-test away from the pinned version
#
# kind: exe (run the installer), msi (msiexec /i ... /qn), msix (added
# through the Store's PackageManager), zip (a portable program, unpacked into
# C:\Games\<name as a slug>); a program starting with "tray:" has no main
# window -- it must still be running afterwards; "cli:" is a command-line
# program, tested by its smoke command alone. "dxvk" among the registry values
# installs DXVK's DLLs with native overrides, as the image's sg-install-d3d
# does. A program starting with "accept:" may put up a dialog first (a
# Unity game's settings): its default button is pressed. An
# "itch:USER/GAME/UPLOAD-ID" URL is an itch.io free download.
# Nothing downloaded here is ever committed or shipped: users install their
# own software (Microsoft 365, Teams and Edge included).
# Installers are downloaded to ~/.cache/sg-compat, checked against the pinned
# hash, and never committed or shipped: users install their own software.
# The hashes were pinned from the official sites over HTTPS on 2026-09-24
# (the entries after LibreOffice on 2026-09-25). Steam's installer URL is not
# versioned: when Valve replaces it, re-pin its hash.
# "OUTER.zip!INNER" is an installer inside a zip (the hash is the zip's).
